00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.869
What is it exactly?

00:06:00.869 --> 00:06:02.910
WILL CURRAN: Yeah, so the
public datasets program

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:06.810
launched just over a year
ago our Big Next Conference

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.490
in 2016.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.150
And what it is is
a program where

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:15.120
Google Cloud hosts open
datasets in BigQuery, and also

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.830
Google Cloud Storage.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:22.024
And we do a significant
amount of ETL on the datasets.

00:06:22.024 --> 00:06:23.940
We're not just mirroring
them in Google Cloud.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.790
We're improving accessibility.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.430
So for example,
some of the datasets

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:33.780
that we have ingested from
data.gov, Mike's team's

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.360
done some ETL on those to
get those into BigQuery.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.340
And what that does
for users is, it

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:41.910
allows them via
serverless access,

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:45.590
to query those datasets
via the UI or command line.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.560
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.281
What is ETL?

00:06:47.281 --> 00:06:49.530
WILL CURRAN: Mike, you want
to jump in and cover that,

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:50.620
since that's your part?

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:51.411
MIKE HAMBERG: Yeah.

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:54.210
That's extract,
transform, and load--

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.960
so basically, getting the
data from the source, doing

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.090
whatever we need to
do it make it pretty--

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.580
sometimes that's optimizing
it, or denormalizing it,

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.030
or whatever needs to happen--

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:05.430
and then, loading it, in
this case, into BigQuery.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.346
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:07:06.346 --> 00:07:08.790
So at the end, we end
up with a dataset that

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.150
is ready to be used
by anyone, and that

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:15.720
is available either on BigQuery
on Google Cloud Storage.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:16.562
Is that right?

00:07:16.562 --> 00:07:17.270
WILL CURRAN: Yes.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.145
MIKE MANDEL: Awesome.

